WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.446
Why the internet's

00:00:01.258 --> 00:00:02.413
core protocol was

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.392
never patented

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:05.344
Vint Cerf co-designed

00:00:05.156 --> 00:00:06.359
TCP IP with

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:06.984
Bob Kahn in

00:00:06.795 --> 00:00:08.045
the 1970s

00:00:08.184 --> 00:00:09.174
Their paper came

00:00:08.986 --> 00:00:10.684
out in May 1974

00:00:11.206 --> 00:00:12.373
Why no patent

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.243
They didn't know

00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:14.021
who their allies

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:14.823
would be twenty-five

00:00:14.635 --> 00:00:15.460
years later

00:00:15.555 --> 00:00:16.297
so the only

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:17.028
way to guarantee

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.865
access was to

00:00:17.677 --> 00:00:18.538
open it up

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.272
Now 83

00:00:20.379 --> 00:00:21.522
Cerf left Google

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.206
after more than

00:00:22.018 --> 00:00:23.291
twenty years and

00:00:23.103 --> 00:00:24.046
is helping start

00:00:23.858 --> 00:00:24.565
Tolero

00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:25.933
building software for

00:00:25.745 --> 00:00:26.900
an internet between

00:00:26.712 --> 00:00:27.525
planets

00:00:28.062 --> 00:00:29.076
Full story on

00:00:28.887 --> 00:00:29.783
the dashboard
